    "answer": {
      "short": "$k=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt3}{9}$. At the common point, equate both the ordinates and tangent gradients.",
      "worked": "Let the point of contact have $x=t>0$. Equal tangent gradients and equal ordinates give\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\frac{k}{t^2}&=-2t\\\\k&=2t^3\\\\\\frac{k}{t}&=1-t^2\\\\2t^2&=1-t^2\\\\3t^2&=1\\\\t&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt3}\\\\k&=\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt3}{9}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
